Group:
	•	Group revenues decreased to $5.40bn in Q3-26 from $5.78bn in Q3-25, a decrease of 6.7% YoY (2.8% decrease on a same-store/LFL basis; 6.6% on constant currency).
	•	Group gross profit decreased to $854.8m in Q3-26 from $919.7m in Q3-25, a decrease of 7.1% YoY (4.1% decrease on a same-store basis).
	•	New vehicle units sold decreased to 55,259 in Q3-26 from 57,269 in Q3-25, a decrease of 3.5% YoY (1.2% decrease on a same-store basis).
	•	Used vehicle (retail) units sold decreased to 53,343 in Q3-26 from 59,574 in Q3-25, a decrease of 10.5% YoY (8.5% decrease on a same-store basis).
	•	Parts & service gross profit decreased to $392.0m (55.9% margin) in Q3-26 from $407.6m in Q3-25, a decrease of 3.8% YoY (essentially flat on a same-store basis at +0.1%).
	•	Global economic environment and challenging market conditions continued to weigh on new and used vehicle retail performance.
	•	CEO Daryl Kenningham commentary: “We’re pleased to have closed the Hennessy acquisition and grateful to the Hennessy family for 62 years of excellent stewardship. This acquisition aligns with our strategy to focus on high-revenue, premium brand stores in growing markets… Our focus on operating execution was evident in the third quarter. Year-over-year growth rates improved across key same store operating metrics compared to the second quarter, despite challenging market conditions. Importantly, in the U.S. we grew same-store customer pay revenue and repair orders 3% and 4% year-over-year, respectively, and continued to benefit from the cost-cutting actions we took earlier this year.”
	•	All-time record U.S. customer-pay revenues and repair order count; U.S. SG&A expenses decreased 6.0% YoY (adjusted SG&A –5.4%).
	•	Diluted Adj. EPS (from continuing operations) of $9.36 for Q3-26 was below street consensus of ~$9.50 (miss of ~$0.14) and down from $10.45 in Q3-25; GAAP diluted EPS from continuing operations was $8.59 (vs. $1.02 in Q3-25, heavily impacted by prior-year impairments).
	•	Total debt increased to $3.89bn as of 30 September 2026 from $3.70bn at 31 December 2025 (floorplan notes payable, net $2.12bn); cash and cash equivalents rose sharply to $881.5m. Disposition proceeds support the ongoing commitment to reduce leverage (completed U.S. dispositions of ~$235m since quarter-end, with a further ~$125m under definitive agreement, totaling ~$360m).
UK Focus:
	•	During the quarter, disposed of a Volkswagen and an Audi dealership in the UK (~$100m annualized revenues); YTD UK dealership disposition annualized revenues ~$495m.
	•	Reached agreement with Jaguar Land Rover to revoke prior election to terminate 10 JLR franchise agreements (retaining the five remaining UK JLR stores).
	•	Expanded UK network with Geely (two of three planned locations open; third expected by December 2026); subsequent to quarter-end, agreed with Chery to open an Omoda & Jaecoo location (also expected by December 2026).
	•	YTD acquired and integrated three UK dealership operations with total expected annual revenues of ~$135m.
	•	UK revenues decreased to $1.41bn in Q3-26 from $1.50bn in Q3-25, a decrease of 6.6% YoY (6.2% on constant currency); same-store performance stronger in key areas (e.g., UK new vehicle retail units +1.9% reported / +8.1% same-store; used vehicle retail GP PRU +15.7% / +13.9% same-store; parts & service revenues –2.4% reported / +6.4% same-store).
	•	UK gross profit decreased to $197.1m in Q3-26 from $204.7m in Q3-25, a decrease of 3.7% YoY.
Corporate Development / Other:
	•	Completed the acquisition of 10 high-volume, high-margin dealerships from Hennessy Automobile Companies on 19 October 2026 (post-quarter), expanding Atlanta presence to 15 dealerships with expected annual revenues of ~$1.7bn. YTD U.S. acquisitions (inclusive of Hennessy) total 14 dealership operations with ~$2bn expected annual revenues.
	•	No share repurchases in Q3-26; YTD repurchased 205,190 shares (~1.7% of shares outstanding at 1 January 2026) at an average price of $353.08 for a total cost of $72.4m. As of 30 September 2026, ~11.95m shares outstanding and $306.3m remaining under the repurchase authorization.
	•	Company continues portfolio reshaping via dispositions of non-core stores and integration of higher-quality acquisitions, with cost actions supporting operating execution.
Share Price:
	•	Diluted Adj. EPS of $9.36 missed consensus ($9.50); revenue of $5.40bn missed consensus ($5.58bn). (Market reaction shortly after release to be confirmed based on open/trading.)
